{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/255436.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS KENT-819D61: Kent-819D61. Roman. Coin. Billon Antoninianus barbarous radiate copy of Claudius II. Reverse view."]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["moneta"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["metallo (moneta)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["270-272 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Kent (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Iscrizione o legenda"]},"value":{"none":["(IMP CL)AVD(IVS AVG) ; (CO)NSECR(A)T(IO)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["Deified 270AD. Roman, Claudius II (268-270AD) billon Antoninianus, barbarous radiate copy. Obverse: Radiate bust right - not draped. Inscription: (IMP CL)AVD(IVS AVG). Reverse: Eagle - Emporer's ascent to join the Gods Inscription: (CO)NSECR(A)T(IO). Length 20.4mm, Width 17.2mm, Thickness 1.6mm, Diameter 20.4mm, Weight 1.6g. Die axis 250 deg. or 11 o'clock. Oval shape with some of the legend struck off the flan. Attractive grey/brown patina - possible remains of patinated silvered surface, but some wear. Ref. Coins of England and the UK, Spink 2009, page 59 No. 567 or page 79 No. 749 and Identifying Roman Coins, Richard Reece & Simon James, Seaby 1986 reprinted 1994, page 25 No.s 47 & 56"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["KENT-819D61"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["255436"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: None, Geoff Burr, 2009-05-11 14:57:12, CC BY-SA 2.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/recor